🟢 5. Kubernetes Storage — MUST LEARN
Kubernetes Storage — Persistent application data
PersistentVolume (PV) — Cluster-level storage resource
PersistentVolumeClaim (PVC) — Request for storage
StorageClass — Storage type and dynamic provisioning
Dynamic Provisioning — Automatically creating storage


# Kubernetes Storage — Persistent Application Data
Kubernetes Storage ka use application ka data save rakhne ke liye hota hai.
Normally Pod delete hone par uska temporary data delete ho sakta hai.
Example:
MySQL Pod → Database data → Pod deleted ❌ → Data lost ❌
Storage use karne par:
MySQL Pod → Storage → Pod deleted ❌ → Data safe ✅

2. PersistentVolume (PV)
PV = Actual storage
PV Kubernetes cluster mein available storage hota hai.
Example:
// PV = 10 GB Storage
👉 Simple: PV matlab storage jo available hai.

3. PersistentVolumeClaim (PVC)
PVC = Storage ki request
Application bolti hai:
"Mujhe 5 GB storage chahiye."
PVC ye request Kubernetes ko deta hai.
PVC → "Mujhe 5 GB chahiye"
PV  → "Mere paas 5 GB hai"
👉 Simple: PVC matlab storage maangna.

4. StorageClass
StorageClass = Storage ka type/configuration
Ye batata hai ki kis type ka storage use karna hai.
Example:
SSD Storage
HDD Storage
Fast Storage
👉 Simple: StorageClass matlab storage ka type.

5. Dynamic Provisioning
Dynamic Provisioning = Storage automatically create hona

Agar application PVC ke through storage maangti hai, Kubernetes StorageClass ki help se storage automatically create kar sakta hai.

PVC
 ↓
StorageClass
 ↓
Storage automatically created
 ↓
PV

👉 Simple: Dynamic Provisioning matlab manually PV banane ki zarurat nahi, Kubernetes automatically storage create kar deta hai.


