🟢 6. Configuration & Secrets — MUST LEARN
 ConfigMap is used to store non-sensitive configuration data, while Secret is used to store sensitive data like passwords, tokens, and API keys.

# ConfigMaps — Non-sensitive application configuration
ConfigMap Kubernetes ka object hai jo application ki non-sensitive configuration values ko store karta hai. Isse configuration ko application ke code/image se alag rakha ja sakta hai.

Practical example:
Maan lo application ko pata hona chahiye ki woh development environment mein run ho rahi hai aur backend server ka URL kya hai.

apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: app-config
data:
  APP_ENV: development
  SERVER_URL: http://backend:8080

# Secrets — Passwords, tokens and sensitive configuration
Secret Kubernetes ka object hai jo sensitive information ko store karne ke liye use hota hai, jaise passwords, API tokens aur credentials.

Practical example:
Maan lo application ko database se connect karne ke liye password chahiye:

apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: db-secret
type: Opaque
stringData:
  username: admin
  password: mypassword

> ConfigMap	         Secret
Non-sensitive data	Sensitive data
App settings	        Passwords
URLs	               API tokens
Environment values	Credentials
> ConfigMap = "Application ko kaise run karna hai"
> Secret = "Application ko access karne ke liye private information"


# Environment Variables — Passing configuration to containers
Environment Variables Kubernetes mein configuration values ko container ke andar pass karne ka ek simple way hai. Application in values ko directly read kar sakti hai.

Practical example:

containers:
  - name: app
    image: nginx
    env:
      - name: APP_ENV
        value: "production"
      - name: APP_PORT
        value: "8080"

Container ke andar:

APP_ENV=production
APP_PORT=8080

Application in values ko use kar sakti hai.

Environment Variables ko ConfigMap ya Secret se bhi provide kar sakte hain:

ConfigMap → Environment Variable → Container
Secret    → Environment Variable → Container


# Annotations — Additional metadata and configuration
Annotations Kubernetes objects ke saath additional information/metadata store karne ke liye use hoti hain. Ye information Kubernetes tools, controllers, monitoring systems, ya other applications use kar sakte hain.

Practical example:

apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: my-app
  annotations:
    description: "My production application"
    owner: "devops-team"
spec:
  containers:
    - name: app
      image: nginx

Yahan:

description → application ke baare mein extra information
owner       → kis team/application ka hai

Annotations ka common practical use Ingress controllers, monitoring tools, deployment tools etc. ke configuration mein hota hai.
